      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**Long-term backfill runs** — one row per run in `ltb_runs` (migration 075), written best-effort by `receivers.scheduling.ltb_run_metrics` at the end of the 04:00 daily backstop and each 15-min reconnection tick that had candidates. The failure this exists to show is **silent**: a run that stops on the wall-clock cap just recovers less each night while every pipeline dashboard stays green. *Recovered* = slots whose download brought back ≥1 file; *nothing on receiver* = reached the receiver, no file there (NOT a recovery). **Data path:** the LTB runs on rek-d01 and writes rek-d01's `gps_health`; this datasource on grafana.vedur.is reads **pgdev**, which receives the row only via the `mirror_host` dual-write in `database_factory` — and only once migration 075 is applied on pgdev too. Until then these panels are populated on the dev Grafana only.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.0.0",
      "title": "",
      "type": "text"
    },
